{"id":"u-a57b120e-421e-4cb6-800b-a7ed35c3c67f","src":"community","title":"The Iron Architect","author":"Mike Fitz 💪","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/0ROqQn-10weekhypertrophyboostcampfinal","desc":"Iron Architect is a high-volume bodybuilding program built for advanced trainees who want maximum hypertrophy, better joint longevity, and smarter recovery without chasing arbitrary powerbuilding numbers. \n\nInstead of relying on high-risk barbell movements, it prioritizes stable machines, cables, lever arms, hack/leg press patterns, and controlled execution to create high mechanical tension with less joint and spinal stress.\n\nThe program runs on a rolling 9-day microcycle instead of a rigid 7-day week:\n\nLower A, Push A, Rest, Pull A, Lower B, Rest, Push B, Pull B, Rest\n\nThis 2-days-on, 1-day-off structure prevents the usual cumulative fatigue wall by forcing recovery before performance drops. Each session is designed so you can train hard, recover, and come back with full output instead of dragging fatigue across the week.\n\nA key feature is the leg-day activation sequence. Every lower session starts with leg extensions followed by leg curls. This warms up the knees, quads, hamstrings, and surrounding tissues before heavier compounds. By pre-loading the target muscles first, you can push hack squats, leg presses, RDLs, and hip-dominant movements with better control, less ego loading, and a stronger mind-muscle connection.\n\nBack training is split intentionally. Pull A focuses on upper back thickness, traps, rhomboids, and rear delts. Pull B focuses more on lat width and arm growth. This prevents the common issue of building plenty of mid-back thickness while undertraining lower-lat width, helping create a wider and more complete V-taper.\n\nPush training is also structured to manage shoulder stress. Pressing volume is grouped into dedicated push sessions, while heavy overhead work is limited. More emphasis is placed on chest-supported pressing, cables, side delts, rear delts, and shoulder-friendly movement patterns to build width and roundness without beating up the shoulder joint.\n\nOverall, Iron Architect is built around one idea: train hard, but train intelligently. Maximize stimulus, minimize junk volume, protect the joints, and recover well enough to progress.","level":["Advanced","Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":100,"joins":1,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-05-23T23:34:29.950Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Lower A: Quad Heavy / Posterior Volume","Push A: Chest Heavy / Delts","Pull A: Upper Back & Traps Heavy / Rear Delts","Lower B: Glute & Hamstring Heavy / Quad Volume","Push B: Shoulder Heavy / Chest Volume","Pull B: Lat Focus / Arms & Side Delts Pump"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":20,"x":2}]},{"n":"Seated Hamstring Curl","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":2}]},{"n":"Hack Squat","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hip Thrust (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":2}]},{"n":"Seated Calf Raise","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Tricep Rope Push Down (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":2}]},{"n":"Neutral Grip Dumbbell Bench Press","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":20,"x":2}]},{"n":"Incline Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pec Deck (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":20,"x":2}]},{"n":"Cable Crunch","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Shrug (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":15,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown (Neutral Grip)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":2}]},{"n":"Rear Delt Fly (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":25,"x":2}]},{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":20,"x":2}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":25,"x":2}]},{"n":"S